The OpenVPN community project team is proud to release OpenVPN 2.3.7. It=20
can be downloaded from here:

<http://openvpn.net/index.php/open-source/downloads.html>

This release contains bugfixes in the MTU handling for peer-id (TLS=20
floating), so if you connect to a server that supports it you should=20
install this upgrade. In addition TLS version negotiation is again=20
enabled by default. There are also a number of small bug fixes and=20
enhancements. A full list of changes is available here:

<https://community.openvpn.net/openvpn/wiki/ChangesInOpenvpn23>

